\label{def:flag-type}


A \emph{flag type} $\sigma$ is a simple graph on a finite label set $T$. It
describes the labeled ``root'' every flag of type $\sigma$ must carry.

\label{def:empty-labeled-graph}



The trivial carrier: the type $\sigma$ itself on $T$ with the identity
embedding. Its isomorphism class is the empty flag.

\label{def:flag-eqv}



The relation $G \sim_f G'$: ``there exists a labeled-graph isomorphism
$G \simeq_f G'$''. Flags are its equivalence classes.

\label{def:induced-labeled-subgraph}



The labeled subgraph of $G$ induced on a chosen vertex set $S$ containing all
labeled vertices --- the canonical way to cut out a sub-flag on $S$.

\label{def:labeled-graph-list}



A $t$-tuple of labeled graphs, the $i$-th on vertex type $V_i$; the
pre-quotient form of a flag list.

\label{thm:eqv-quot-list-flaglist}



The quotient of labeled-graph lists is equivalent to the tuple of flags: taking
isomorphism classes commutes with the $\mathrm{Fin}\,t$-indexed product.

\label{def:labeled-graph-count}



$\mathrm{labeledGraphCount}\,H\,G$ is the number of induced labeled subgraphs
of the host $G$ that are labeled-isomorphic to $H$.

\label{lem:density-iso-invariant}



Labeled-graph density is invariant under $\simeq_f$ in both arguments. This is
the well-definedness fact that lets density descend to flags.

\label{lem:subflag-density-values}



The empty flag has density $1$ in every flag; a flag has density $1$ in
itself; two distinct flags of the same size have density $0$ in each other.

\label{def:basis-vector}



$\mathrm{basisVector}\,F$ is the unit vector supported on the single flag $F$;
every construction reduces to these.

\label{thm:quot-mul-density}



In $\mathcal{A}^\sigma$, $[\![F]\!]\cdot[\![G]\!] = [\![\,\mathrm{flagMul}\,F\,G\,]\!]$:
the ring product of two flags is the class of their density expansion.

\label{def:flag-with-size}



$\mathrm{FlagWithSize}\,\sigma\,n = \mathrm{Flag}\,\sigma\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,n)$:
a flag on the fixed $n$-element carrier.

\label{def:flag-expansion}



$\mathrm{flagExpansion}\,F\,\ell = \sum_{F'} d_1(F;F')\,\cdot F'$, the averaged
expansion of $F$ onto size-$\ell$ flags.

\label{def:zero-set}



The set of all averaging relations $\mathrm{zeroElement}\,F\,\ell$ (with
$|F| \le \ell$); its span is the zero space.

\label{def:flag-vector-eqv}



$f \sim_v g$ iff $f - g \in \mathrm{ZeroSpace}\,\sigma$: the two vectors
represent the same flag-algebra element.

\label{thm:quot-hom}



The quotient map $[\![\,\cdot\,]\!]$ commutes with addition, multiplication,
scalar multiplication, and finite sums.

\label{thm:basis-quot-eq-sum}



In the algebra, $[\![F]\!] = \sum_{F'} d_1(F;F')\,[\![F']\!]$ over size-$\ell$
flags: the averaging relation written as a $[\![\,\cdot\,]\!]$ identity.

\label{thm:flag-algebra-nontrivial}



$0 \ne 1$ in $\mathcal{A}^\sigma$: the flag algebra is nontrivial (so its
$\mathrm{CommRing}$ structure is not the zero ring).

\label{def:unlabel}



$\mathrm{unlabel}$ drops the type embedding of a single flag, returning its
underlying graph as an unlabeled ($\emptyset$-type) flag.

\label{lem:downward-well-defined}



The unlabeling map sends the zero space of $\sigma$ into the zero space of the
empty type, so it descends to the quotient algebra.

\label{def:downward}



$[\![\,\cdot\,]\!]_0 : \mathcal{A}^\sigma \to \mathcal{A}^\emptyset$ is the
$\mathbb{R}$-linear map induced by $F \mapsto w(F)\cdot \mathrm{unlabel}\,F$;
it averages a labeled element over all unlabelings.

\label{thm:downward-linear}



$[\![f+f']\!]_0 = [\![f]\!]_0 + [\![f']\!]_0$ and
$[\![r\cdot f]\!]_0 = r\cdot[\![f]\!]_0$: downward is $\mathbb{R}$-linear.

\label{thm:downward-empty}



On $\mathcal{A}^\emptyset$ there is nothing to unlabel, so
$[\![f]\!]_0 = f$.

\label{def:isomorphism-count}



The number of label placements on the same underlying graph as $G$ that are
flag-isomorphic to $G$.

\label{def:label-extensions}



For an unlabeled flag $F$, the finset of all $\sigma$-labeled flags of the same
size whose unlabeling is $F$ --- the ways to re-add a labelling.

\label{lem:downward-flag-sum}



$\mathrm{downwardFlag}\,F \sim_v \sum_{G} d_1(F;G)\cdot\mathrm{downwardFlag}\,G$
over size-$\ell$ flags --- the averaging expansion driving well-definedness.

\label{lem:downward-zero-element}



$\mathrm{downwardFlagVector}$ sends each generating relation
$\mathrm{zeroElement}\,F\,\ell$ into the zero space of the empty type.

\label{lem:downward-factor-pos}



$w(F) > 0$ for every flag $F$: every flag is realized by at least one label
placement.

\label{thm:flag-nonneg}



Every flag satisfies $[\![F]\!] \ge 0$ --- the base positivity fact from which
sum-of-squares bounds are assembled.

\label{thm:sos-nonneg}



If $M \succeq 0$ (positive semidefinite) then
$\mathrm{flagQuadraticForm}\,M\,v \ge 0$ in the semantic cone.

\label{def:hom}



$\mathrm{Hom}\,\sigma = \mathcal{A}^\sigma \to_{\mathbb{R}\text{-alg}}
\mathbb{R}$, the underlying $\mathbb{R}$-algebra homomorphisms; a positive
homomorphism is such a map that is additionally nonnegative on flags.

\label{def:flag-algebra-vec}



$\mathrm{FlagAlgebraVec}\,\sigma\,n = \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal{A}^\sigma$,
the variables of a quadratic form.

\label{lem:positivehom-basisvector-nonneg}



$0 \le \varphi[\![F]\!]$ for every positive homomorphism $\varphi$ and flag
$F$ --- the defining positivity, restated as $0 \le \cdot$.

\label{lem:order-monotone-sides}



Adding a fixed element on either side preserves the semantic order; these
register as the \texttt{AddLeftMono}/\texttt{AddRightMono} instances.

\label{def:flag-seq}



A \emph{flag sequence} is a sequence $\mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{FinFlag}\,\sigma$
of flags, typically of growing size.

\label{def:flag-density-space}



The compact, metrizable space of density profiles $\mathrm{FinFlag}\,\sigma \to
[0,1]$ (a Tychonoff cube); the ambient space of the limit semantics.

\label{def:converges-to}



$\mathrm{ConvergesTo}\,s\,a$ says the flag sequence $s$ has strictly increasing
sizes and its subgraph-density profile converges pointwise to the limit $a$.

\label{def:positive-hom-space}



The range of the profile map; shown to be closed, hence compact and
measurable.

\label{thm:limit-is-hom}



Any convergent flag-sequence density limit is the profile of some positive
homomorphism.

\label{thm:hom-is-limit}



Conversely every positive homomorphism arises as a convergent flag-sequence
limit.

\label{thm:square-downward-nonneg}



$[\![f\cdot f]\!]_0 \ge 0$ for every $f$: the downward image of a square is
nonnegative.

\label{thm:cauchy-schwarz}



$[\![f\cdot f]\!]_0 \cdot [\![g\cdot g]\!]_0 \ge [\![f\cdot g]\!]_0^2$, the key
inequality behind semidefinite flag-algebra density bounds.

\label{def:flag-density-seq}



$n \mapsto (F \mapsto d_1(F; s_n))$, the profile whose limit defines the
semantics.

\label{def:positivehom-topmf}



The distribution on size-$\ell$ flags whose mass at $F$ is $\varphi[\![F]\!]$;
$\varphi$'s random model at scale $\ell$.

\label{lem:integral-density-div}



The expected $F$-density under a large flag's measure equals the normalized
downward density ratio; the finite-level identity behind Lemma~3.11.

\label{lem:measure-support}



The weak limit of a convergent flag sequence's probability measures is
concentrated on the positive-homomorphism space.

\label{def:prob-measure-witness}



The chosen random-extension measure $\mathbb{P}[\varphi_0]$, the witness of
Theorem~\ref{thm:random-hom-measure}.

\label{thm:prob-measure-spec}



Integrating $\varphi \mapsto \varphi(f)$ against $\mathbb{P}[\varphi_0]$
recovers $\varphi_0[\![f]\!]_0 / \varphi_0[\![1]\!]_0$.

\label{lem:positivehom-one-downward-pos}



If $\varphi_0\langle\sigma\rangle_0 > 0$ then $\varphi_0[\![1]\!]_0 > 0$, the
denominator in the normalized downward value.

\label{def:sym2-labeled-graph}



The typed version: an edge set together with a graph embedding of a decoded
type $\sigma$; decodes to an abstract $\mathrm{LabeledGraph}$.

\label{def:deg-key}



A cheap $O(n)$ isomorphism invariant --- edge count paired with the sorted
degree sequence --- used to prefilter before the expensive isomorphism test.

\label{thm:deg-key-iso-invariant}



Equivalent graphs share the cheap key, justifying its use as a deduplication
prefilter.

\label{def:fast-iso-decidable}



The high-priority $\mathrm{Decidable}$ instance for flag equivalence backed by
the fast test; it makes $\mathrm{Fintype}$-based flag enumeration tractable.

\label{thm:downward-compute}



A computable downward normalizing factor on edge-set flags, proved equal to the
abstract $\mathrm{downwardNormalizingFactor}$ on the decoded flag.

\label{def:sym2-count}



The computable numerators of the densities: the number of vertex-disjoint
placements of a flag list inside a host, empty-typed and $\sigma$-typed.

\label{def:deg-seq}



The sorted degree sequence of an edge-set graph, the main part of the cheap
isomorphism key.

\label{thm:mantel-hom}



For every positive homomorphism $\varphi$ with $\varphi(K_3) = 0$ (a
triangle-free limit), $\varphi(K_2) \le \tfrac12$.
